    "model": "Frame: Draw a landscape rectangle about 15 cm by 10 cm. Title it Sketch Map of OS Map, Macroom, with a north arrow in the top right corner and a rough scale.\nProportions: Keep the frame about one and a half times wider than it is tall, like the map. Draw it freehand and neatly, not traced.\nBuilt-up area of Macroom: Shade a grey patch in the top right of the frame. Label it Macroom built-up area.\nN22 route: Draw a thick green line. It runs from the top left, east along the top of the frame into Macroom. It then turns south through Hartnett's Cross and runs down the right side to the bottom right edge. Label it N22.\nR584 route: Draw a thick orange line. It starts at the left edge near the bottom, runs north-east through Toon Bridge, then east along the north shore of the reservoir. It ends at the N22 near Hartnett's Cross east of Macroom. Label it R584.\nElectricity transmission line: Draw a dashed line with small pylon dots across the top right corner, north-east of Macroom. Label it Electricity transmission line.\nPost office: Draw a small green square marked PO in Macroom, in the top right. Label it Post office.\nOverall: All five features sit in their correct relative positions, with a key.",
    "model_source": "sonnet-figure",
