    "model": "Named city – Kolkata:\nKolkata was founded in 1690 by the British East India Company as a port on the Hooghly river.\nIt was the capital of British India until 1911, which drew administration and jobs to the city.\nIts jute and engineering industries attracted migrants from Bihar, Odisha and rural Bengal.\nThe Bengal famine of 1943 drove millions of rural people towards the city.\nPartition in 1947 brought refugees, and the 1971 Bangladesh Liberation War brought a further wave.\nNatural increase adds to the population, since births exceed deaths.\nThe city has regional primacy in eastern India, and its jobs, schools and hospitals pull in migrants.\nCensus 2011 gave an urban agglomeration of about 14.1 million people.",
