    "label": "1A(v)",
    "marks": 4,
    "model": "Carbonation: rainwater absorbs carbon dioxide from the air and soil and forms a weak carbonic acid.\nThis weak acid reacts with the calcium carbonate in limestone and turns it into soluble calcium bicarbonate, which is carried away in solution.",
