    "label": "2A(iv)",
    "marks": 4,
    "model": "Convection currents in the mantle drag on the underside of the lithosphere and move the plates.\nHeat from the core and radioactive decay warms the rock of the asthenosphere, which rises, cools and sinks again, creating circular convection cells.",
