    "label": "9A(v)",
    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Impact 1: Tariffs and customs barriers. If Ireland left the EU single market, customs duties would apply to exports to EU states, raising their price and reducing competitiveness.\nImpact 2: Extra paperwork and delays. Separate customs checks and certification would slow the movement of agricultural and industrial goods, adding cost for exporters.",
