    "model": "Frame: draw a ruled rectangle 12.7 cm wide by 8.2 cm tall, with four drawn sides. Title it Sketch of the aerial photograph.\nRiver: draw it as a wide band entering at the top about 6.8 to 8 cm across, flowing down the centre of the frame, narrowing slightly and curving to the left at about 5 cm down, then widening into the large harbour in the bottom left corner. Label it River.\nLarge historical ruin in the middle ground: draw a small block with a cross or broken wall on the east bank of the river, at about 8 cm across and 3.9 cm down from the top. Label it Historical ruin.\nEmergency services depot in the left background: draw a rectangular building in the top left at about 3.8 cm across and 1.1 cm down from the top. Label it Emergency services depot.\nCarpark in the left foreground: draw a rectangle in the bottom left at about 2 cm across and 0.5 cm up from the bottom edge, with parking lines. Label it Carpark.\nAdd a key naming the four features.",
