    "model": "The low-lying land beside the river in the centre background could flood, which would threaten the factory and its stock.\nThe dual carriageway in the left background can be reached only by narrower local roads, so lorries would add traffic and congestion on these roads.\nTrees and woodland along the river bank in the centre background would have to be cleared, which would damage wildlife habitats and bring objections from environmental groups.\nHousing in the right background and the left background lies close to the site, so residents would object to noise, heavy traffic and pollution.\nThe river could be polluted by waste from the factory, which would harm fish and wildlife downstream.\nThe scenic riverside fields are valued as an amenity, so planning permission for the factory might be refused or delayed.\nThe hospital in the left background needs quiet and clean air, so building work and lorry traffic nearby would cause problems for patients.",
