    "model": "Absence of settlement – Kings Mountain, G 720 450:\nThe area at G 720 450 on Kings Mountain is high mountain land, with spot heights such as 466 metres and 566 metres on the map.\nThe contour lines are very close together, which shows slopes that are too steep for building houses or farming.\nHigh land is cold, wet and exposed to wind, so it is an unattractive place to live.\nThe soils are thin and poor, so the land supports only rough grazing and no farms with farmhouses.\nNo roads or tracks are shown inside the area, and the nearest road runs along the foot of the mountain at about G 720 427.\nNo black squares or dots, which mark buildings, appear on the upland slopes, whereas houses cluster on the lower land near Lislahelly and Glen Lower.\nBlue streams drain steeply off the mountain, which shows that the ground is wet and cut by gullies.\nThe area is remote from towns, jobs and services, so no one would choose to settle there.",
    "model_source": "sonnet-long-fix",
