    "model": "High density of settlement – Sligo town, G 695 360:\nSligo town at G 695 360 is built on flat, low-lying land beside the Garavogue River and Sligo Harbour, which makes building easy.\nThe grey shading and the dense network of streets on the map show a large built-up area with many closely packed buildings.\nThe N4, N15 and N16 national primary routes and the R287, R291 and R292 regional roads converge on the town, which makes it a route focus.\nThe town grew at a bridging point of the Garavogue River where the river enters the sheltered water of Sligo Harbour.\nThe map shows services such as post offices, hospitals, schools, a fire station and tourist information, which attract people to live in the town.\nA railway line reaches the town centre from the west at about G 686 360, which gives good transport links for people and goods.\nSligo Abbey and a megalithic tomb in the town centre attract tourists, which supports jobs and population.\nSligo is the largest town on the map and serves a large rural hinterland, so it has many jobs and a high population, in contrast to the scattered farmhouses in the surrounding countryside.",
