    "model": "Frame: draw a rectangle 12 cm wide by 9 cm high (half scale, so 1 km on the ground is 1 cm; the map is 12 km by 9 km). Title it Sketch map of the Templemore area, scale 1:100 000, with a north arrow. Mark the grid corners: S 04 68 at bottom left and S 16 77 at top right.\nRiver Suir: draw a blue line starting near the top right at S 132 728 (about 9 cm across, 4.8 cm up). Run it south-west to the railway crossing near S 126 720, then south past Aughall More and Kiltillane, through S 120 707 and S 120 700, and finish near the bottom edge at S 119 680 (about 8 cm across, at the base). Label it River Suir.\nLand above 200 m: shade the north-west corner. The shaded area is bounded by the top edge from about 4.5 cm to 8.4 cm across, then the 200 m contour runs down the east side through about 8.2 cm across at 76 km, 7 cm across at 75 km and 6.3 cm across at 74 km, and curves back west to meet the left edge at about 73.5 km (5.5 cm up). It includes Borrisnoe, Kilduff and Devilsbit Mountains. Label it Land above 200 m.\nTemplemore Lake: draw a small blue oval about 0.5 cm by 0.5 cm just west of Templemore town, near S 107 722 (about 6.7 cm across, 4.2 cm up). Label it Templemore Lake.\nRailway line: draw a thick black line from the top right edge near S 160 752 (right edge, 7.5 cm up). Run it south-west to a bend near S 127 721, then turn south through Kiltillane and Greenwood, passing S 120 700 and ending at the bottom edge near S 119 680. Label it Railway.",
