    "model": "Bronze Age (barrow): a barrow is a burial mound built over the grave of an important person.\nIt was made of earth and stones, and the dead person was often buried with pottery or a bronze tool.\nIt shows that people were farming and settled in the area about 4,000 years ago.\nEarly Christian (ringwork): a ringwork is a circular farmstead enclosed by an earth bank and ditch.\nIt protected the people, their house and their cattle from raiders and wild animals.\nIt shows that farming families lived here between about 500 and 1000 AD.\nNorman (moated site): a moated site is a Norman farmstead or manor surrounded by a water-filled ditch.\nThe moat protected the lord's house and his tenants from attack.\nIt shows that the Normans settled and farmed the land here after their arrival in the 12th century.",
