    "label": "9B(ii)",
    "marks": 21,
    "model": "Location – Leixlip, Co. Kildare:\nThe multinational company, Intel, is located at Leixlip, Co. Kildare, beside the M4 motorway west of Dublin.\nReasons for choosing the location:\nLeixlip lies beside the M4 motorway close to Dublin, so workers, supplies and products can move easily by road, and the finished wafers can be flown out from Dublin Airport.\nA large, flat greenfield site was available, which gave room for the fabrication plants and for later expansion.\nMaynooth University is nearby and Trinity College Dublin and University College Dublin are in the city, which gives access to graduates and research links.\nThe Dublin area has a large labour pool from which the company could recruit workers.\nFabrication plants use huge amounts of electricity and water, and Leixlip had a supply of both.\nIreland's low corporation tax of 12.5% and the grants and support offered by IDA Ireland attracted the American company to invest.\nMembership of the EU gives tariff-free access to the single market, and the workforce is English-speaking, which suits an American company.",
