    "label": "9B(iii)",
    "marks": 12,
    "model": "Lower labour costs: wages in the other country may be much lower than in Ireland.\nThe company spends less on making each product, so its costs fall.\nLower costs mean higher profits for the company.\nThe extra profit can be paid to shareholders or reinvested in the business.",
