    "model": "Frame: draw a rectangle 12.7 cm wide by 8.3 cm high, half the length and breadth of the photograph, and give it the title Sketch map of Foxford.\nRiver: draw a double line entering the top edge about 8.7 cm from the left, curving down and left to the bridge about 4.7 cm across and 4 cm down, then running to the left edge about 6 cm down. Label it River Moy.\nConnecting streets: draw two roads meeting in the town centre. One crosses the river bridge at about 4.7 cm across and 4 cm down and runs right to the right edge at about 5 cm down. Label it Main Street. The other runs from the bottom left corner area, about 2 cm across, up to the junction at about 7 cm across and 5 cm down. Label it Church Street.\nIndustrial building: draw a large rectangle in the upper right, about 10 cm across and 2.7 cm down, beside the road. Label it Industrial building.\nWaste ground in right background: shade an irregular patch in the upper right, about 10 cm across and 1.7 cm down, behind the industrial building. Label it Waste ground.",
