    "model": "Frame: Draw a ruled rectangle about 12 cm by 9 cm, portrait (taller than wide), with the title Sketch Map of the Foxford OS Map and a north arrow in the top right.\nLough Cullin: Shade a large lake along the whole west (left) edge of the frame, from the middle down to the lower left, with its edge curving in a little at the lower middle. Label it Lough Cullin.\nGriffins Island: Draw a small island in the top part of the lake near the west edge, about one third of the way down the frame. Label it Griffins Island.\nMixed woodland: Shade a small patch with tree symbols in the south-centre, near Derreenyanimna in the lower left of the frame, just south of the railway. Label it Mixed woodland.\nLand above 200 m: Draw a closed outline around the whole high ground in the top right (north-east) corner of the frame, about one quarter of the width and one quarter of the height of the map. Shade it and label it Land above 200 m.\nClydagh River: Draw one thin blue line starting at the west edge in the lower left, about one fifth of the way up from the bottom, and running south-east to the bottom left of the map. Label it Clydagh River.",
