    "model": "Outline: draw a rectangle 12.7 cm long by 8.3 cm wide with all four sides drawn, and a title Sketch map of Clonmel aerial photograph.\nConnecting streets: draw two streets joining at a junction. One long main road runs across the foreground from the bottom left towards the centre. A second street runs from the centre foreground up through the middle of the town to the background. Label them main road and connecting street.\nRecreational land use: draw a green oval greyhound track in the top centre, and a green pitch in the left middleground. Label them Recreational land use, sports pitch.\nEcclesiastical land use: in the bottom right foreground draw a small church with a tower, set in green grounds. Label it Ecclesiastical land use, church.\nResidential land use: in the bottom left foreground draw a block of small houses in rows along the streets. Label it Residential land use.",
