    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Reason 1: poor land, such as steep mountains, bogs or deserts, makes farming and building difficult.\nExplanation 1: few people can earn a living or settle there, so the area stays sparsely populated.\nReason 2: harsh climate, such as very cold or very dry conditions.\nExplanation 2: hard living conditions discourage people from settling, so population density stays low.",
