    "label": "6A(vi)",
    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Higher spending: people in work earn more and spend more on goods and services, which boosts business sales.\nBusiness growth: firms facing higher demand expand and hire more workers, which strengthens the economy.\nStronger public finances: the government pays out less in unemployment benefits.\nHigher tax revenue: employed people pay income tax and PRSI, so the state collects more money for public services.",
