    "label": "3A",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "(i) Magnitude: The earthquake had a magnitude of 6.1.\n(ii) First plate: Indian plate.\n(ii) Second plate: Eurasian plate.\n(iii) People killed: 1,036 people were killed.\n(iii) People injured: About 2,000 people were injured.\n(iii) Homes destroyed: About 10,000 homes were partially or entirely destroyed.\n(iv) Epicentre: The point on the Earth's surface directly above the focus.\n(iv) Focus: The point underground where the earthquake starts.\n(v) Earthquake-resistant buildings: Buildings are built with flexible frames and strong foundations so they can move with the ground rather than collapse.\n(v) Building codes: Strict building codes require new buildings in earthquake zones to meet these standards.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
    "answerStatus": "written",
    "type": [
     "short-answer"
    ],
    "diagramRelation": "none",
