    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Frame: Draw a landscape rectangle (about 15 cm by 10 cm, sides in the ratio 3:2) to match the shape of the photograph, with a title Sketch map of Cavan from the aerial photograph.\nLake: Draw an oval, shaded blue, in the bottom right corner of the frame. Label it Lake.\nChurch: Draw a cross-shaped church with a tall spire just above the centre of the frame, slightly right of middle. Label it Church.\nWaste ground: Draw a large irregular grey area in the centre foreground, at the bottom middle of the frame, left of the lake. Label it Waste ground.\nCar park: Draw a rectangle on the left of the frame, just above the centre, beside the tennis courts and the large building. Label it Car park.\nTwo connecting streets: Draw two lines meeting at a junction in the left centre, one running down to the bottom left corner and one running across to the church. Label them Main Street and Church Street.\nShow the features in their correct positions and in the same proportions as the photograph, drawn freehand and not traced.",
    "model_source": "sonnet-figure",
    "answerStatus": "written",
