    "label": "9A",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "(i) Wicklow.\n(ii) The farm covers 25 hectares.\n(iii) It will prevent 4,800 tonnes of greenhouse gas emissions a year.\n(iv) It powers about 3,600 homes a year.\nIt prevents 4,800 tonnes of greenhouse gas emissions a year.\n(v) Wind power.\n(vi) Fossil fuels are fuels formed from the remains of dead plants and animals buried over millions of years.\nExamples are coal, oil and natural gas, and they cannot be replaced once used up.\n(vii) Unreliable supply: solar power only works when the sun shines, so energy is not always available.\nBackup or storage systems are then needed, which adds cost.",
