    "marks": 30,
    "model": "Frame: Draw a landscape rectangle (about 15 cm by 10 cm, sides in the ratio 3:2) to match the shape of the photograph, with a title Sketch map of Cavan from the aerial photograph.\nLake: Draw an oval, shaded blue, in the bottom right corner of the frame. Label it Lake.\nChurch: Draw a cross-shaped church with a tall spire just above the centre of the frame, slightly right of middle. Label it Church.\nTennis courts: Draw two or three small red rectangles side by side, left of centre and just above the middle of the frame. Label them Tennis courts.\nRoundabout: Draw a small circle where roads meet at the bottom edge of the frame, right of centre, below the waste ground. Label it Roundabout.\nIndustrial buildings: Draw several large rectangular buildings with flat roofs in the top left corner of the frame, the left background. Label them Industrial buildings.\nShow the features in their correct positions and in the same proportions as the photograph, drawn freehand and not traced.",
