    "model": "Draw a freehand outline of the Indian sub-continent, about a quarter of the page in size, showing its triangular peninsula with the Arabian Sea to the west, the Bay of Bengal to the east and the Himalayas across the north.\nMumbai: a dot on the west coast, labelled Mumbai.\nDelhi: a dot in the north of the country, labelled Delhi.\nGanges River: a line rising in the Himalayas in the north and flowing east to the Bay of Bengal, labelled Ganges River.\nDeccan Plateau: the outline of the upland plateau covering most of southern India, labelled Deccan Plateau.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
