    "label": "4A",
    "marks": 20,
    "model": "Title: Outline Map of Ireland, written at the top of the page.\nOutline of Ireland: The whole island drawn as one continuous irregular coastline filling most of the page.\nWest Region: Its boundary drawn as an outlined area on the western side of the island, named West Region inside the boundary.\nGalway: A dot on the coast at the head of Galway Bay, in the West Region, labelled Galway.\nRiver Corrib: A line flowing south from Lough Corrib into Galway Bay, passing through Galway, labelled River Corrib.\nConnemara Mountains: A shaded area in the west of the West Region near the coast, labelled Connemara Mountains.\nNames may be written on the map or in a key.",
