    "model": "Frame: draw a landscape rectangle 12 cm wide by 9 cm high with all four sides ruled (half the 24 cm by 18 cm map). Title it Sketch Map of Oughterard Area.\nGolf course: shade a small area at the right edge of the frame, east of Oughterard at about M 140 420 where the flag symbol is, and label it Golf Course.\nViewpoint: mark a blue star-burst symbol in the top middle at about M 108 450 beside the Western Way, and label it Viewpoint.\nCycle route: draw a short dashed line in the top left corner at about M 04 44, near the cycle symbol, and label it Cycle Route.\nForestry: shade a dotted green area in the bottom right of the frame, south of Northing 40, along Northing 38 to 39 between Easting 11 and Easting 14 (south of Buffy Lough), and label it Forestry.\nLabel each feature on the sketch or in a key.",
