    "model": "Title: Paris Basin, France, written above the frame.\nDraw a landscape rectangle about a quarter of a page in size with four straight ruled sides.\nDraw the outline of the region as a rounded, saucer-shaped area filling most of the frame, with the English Channel coast along the north-west edge.\nShade the saucer-shaped lowland and label it Paris Basin lowland.\nDraw the River Seine as a continuous line flowing from the south-east of the frame, through the centre, to the Channel coast in the north-west, and label it River Seine.\nMark Paris with a dot in the centre of the frame on the River Seine, and label it Paris.\nMark Le Havre with a dot on the north-west coast where the River Seine meets the Channel, and label it Le Havre.",
    "model_source": "haiku",
