    "label": "4A",
    "marks": 20,
    "model": "Map outline: draw the outline of Italy, a boot shape, about 10 cm tall and drawn freehand. Do not draw Ireland. Give it the title 'Italy'.\nUrban centre 1: put a dot in the north-west and label it 'Milan'.\nUrban centre 2: put a dot on the west coast, about halfway down, and label it 'Rome'.\nRiver: draw a wavy line from the Alps in the north-west to the Adriatic Sea in the north-east, and label it 'River Po'.\nRelief feature: draw the outline of the Alps as a curved shape across the top of the country and label it 'Alps (upland)'.",
    "model_source": "sonnet-figure",
