    "label": "8A(vi)",
    "marks": 8,
    "model": "Advantage one: Renewable energy does not run out.\nExplanation: Sun, wind and water are constantly replaced by nature, so supplies last indefinitely.\nAdvantage two: Renewable energy produces little or no carbon dioxide.\nExplanation: Burning fossil fuels releases greenhouse gases that cause climate change, but renewable sources do not.",
