    "model": "Frame: draw a landscape rectangle 12.7 cm long by 8.4 cm wide with four ruled sides. Title it Sketch map of aerial photograph of Dundalk.\nRiver: draw a wide wavy double line across the top of the frame, from the top left across the upper centre to the top right, and label it River.\nRailway line: draw a long double line (or line with cross ticks) running from the top centre of the frame down through the middle to the bottom right, and label it Railway line.\nResidential land-use area: shade a block of small house shapes along streets in the left middle of the frame, west of the railway line, and label it Residential area.\nRecreational land-use area: draw a rectangle for the sports pitches in the left of the frame, just left of the railway line and below the middle, and label it Recreational area (sports pitches).",
    "model_source": "sonnet-figure",
