    "label": "6A",
    "marks": 30,
    "model": "(i) The U.K.\n(ii) Albania.\n(iii) Countries join the EU to gain access to the single market and its trade benefits.\n(iv) Irish exporters can sell goods across the EU without customs charges between member states.\nIreland receives EU funding for projects such as roads and rural development.\n(v) Member states often disagree on key issues such as migration, which slows down decision-making.\nSlow decisions make it harder for the EU to respond quickly to crises.",
